#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172083 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171889 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5b00f0c-fc7f-5262-b1a3-cdd6c1560cd6" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching a Two-Dimensional Vector Field"}] :question/id #uuid "f0111439-4fd8-5add-b95f-5e783178fd63" :question/math-academy-id "e-9440" :question/problem "Draw a diagram that represents the vector field \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y)= -2xy \\, \\mathbf{i} + x^2 \\, \\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\n at the points $(-2,1), (-1,-2),$ and $(1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "To sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $\\mathbf F(x,y) = -2xy \\, \\mathbf{i} + x^2 \\, \\mathbf{j} \\,\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-2,1) & =-2(-2)(1)\\,i+(-2)^{2}\\,j=4\\,i+4\\,j \\\\ F(-1,-2) & =-2(-1)(-2)\\,i+(-1)^{2}\\,j=-4\\,i+j \\\\ F(1,-1) & =-2(1)(-1)\\,i+{1}^{2}\\,j=2\\,i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](images/cf/cf51cba8548d1f342a9dd5c06b533782feb955fca4b90adfac5b6988d7e2e470.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5b00f0c-fc7f-5262-b1a3-cdd6c1560cd6" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050412}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518833 :question-generator/id #uuid "cec5f635-1600-53d9-9628-ff389755df01" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186172083.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172275 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5b00f0c-fc7f-5262-b1a3-cdd6c1560cd6" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching a Two-Dimensional Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a92a7327-4920-5e27-9447-1c7bf838154d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/17/17e2a819903c4836cbf77cd117939be363525a64